SmartCare v0.5 – Architecture & Refactoring Workbook:

Current Architecture Problems:
| Problem                               | Evidence                                           | Impact                                           | Refactoring                                      |
|---------------------------------------|----------------------------------------------------|--------------------------------------------------|--------------------------------------------------|
| UI mixed with domain logic            | input(), print() inside Appointment                | Hard to test; violates separation of concerns    | Move UI logic to Presentation layer              |
| SQL inside domain classes             | sqlite3 calls inside AppointmentService            | Domain depends on persistence                    | Move SQL to Repository/Persistence layer         |
| Business rules scattered              | Conflict checks in UI + DB layer                   | Inconsistent behaviour                           | Centralise rules in Domain layer                 |
| God-class service                     | ClinicManager handles all use cases                | SRP violation; unmaintainable                    | Split into smaller use-case services             |
| Validation in persistence layer       | DB code checks patient name                        | Wrong responsibility                              | Move validation to Domain layer                  |

Layer Responsibilities:
Presentation Layer -
| Responsibilities               | Must NOT contain                      |
|--------------------------------|---------------------------------------|
| Read input                     | Business rules                        |
| Display output                 | SQL                                   |
| Format messages                | Domain invariants                     |

Service/Application Layer -
| Responsibilities               | Must NOT contain                      |
|--------------------------------|---------------------------------------|
| Coordinate use cases           | SQL                                   |
| Orchestrate workflows          | UI logic                              |
| Call domain objects            | Domain invariants                     |

Domain Layer -
| Responsibilities               | Must NOT contain                      |
|--------------------------------|---------------------------------------|
| Business rules                 | SQL                                   |
| Validation                     | UI formatting                         |
| Status transitions             | Input handling                        |
| Invariants                     | Persistence logic                     |

Repository Layer -
| Responsibilities               | Must NOT contain                      |
|--------------------------------|---------------------------------------|
| Retrieve domain objects        | Business rules                        |
| Save/update domain objects     | UI logic                              |
| Abstract persistence           | Workflow logic                        |

Persistence Layer - 
| Responsibilities               | Must NOT contain                      |
|--------------------------------|---------------------------------------|
| Execute SQLite operations      | Domain logic                          |
| Low-level DB access            | Use-case coordination                 |

Architecture Diagram:
+----------------------+
|   Presentation Layer |
| (UI / CLI / Web)     |
+----------+-----------+
           |
           v
+----------------------+
|   Service Layer      |
| (Use-case orchestration)
+----------+-----------+
           |
           v
+----------------------+
|   Domain Layer       |
| (Entities + Rules)   |
+----------+-----------+
           |
           v
+----------------------+
|   Repository Layer   |
| (Interfaces + Adapters)
+----------+-----------+
           |
           v
+----------------------+
|   Persistence Layer  |
| (SQLite / DB driver) |
+----------------------+

SOLID Review:
| Principle | Relevant? | Evidence                                      | Decision                                       |
|-----------|-----------|-----------------------------------------------|------------------------------------------------|
| SRP       | Yes       | ClinicManager handles all use cases           | Split into smaller services                    |
| OCP       | Mild      | Hard-coded status transitions                 | Domain OK; persistence may need abstraction    |
| LSP       | No        | No inheritance hierarchy in v0.5              | Not applicable                                 |
| ISP       | Yes       | Repository interface has 20 methods           | Split into smaller interfaces                  |
| DIP       | Yes       | AppointmentService imports sqlite3 directly   | Introduce repository abstraction               |

AI Architecture Review:
| AI Suggestion            | Observed Problem? | Decision | Reason                                           | Verification                          |
|--------------------------|-------------------|----------|--------------------------------------------------|---------------------------------------|
| Microservices            | Yes               | Reject   | SmartCare is small; monolith is simpler          | Requirements show single-clinic scope |
| Event bus                | Yes               | Reject   | No async workflows or distributed events         | No FR/NFR support                     |
| Six interfaces           | Partial           | Defer    | Over-engineered now; may be useful later         | UML + scope review                    |
| Dependency injection     | Partial           | Defer    | Useful only if system grows                      | Current codebase too small            |
| Repository abstraction   | No                | Keep     | Needed for DIP + testability                     | Matches v0.5 architecture             |
